{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403892-a-different-type-of-archmage-hack","id":1403892,"title":"A different type of Archmage hack.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-21T15:20:09-07:00","id":1403892,"title":"A different type of Archmage hack.","content":"Hello! I've been doing a lot of thinking about archmages, and no matter what I've thought of, it wouldn't ever be something that should be added to a game that uses 5th dot spheres. I think I've come up with something a bit different, sort of like stapling a bonus onto an entire sphere, making it an archsphere?<br /> <br /> Rather than a 6-9 archmage system, give them multiple choices of a single sixth dot.<br /> <br /> These sort of feel more awe inspiring effect-wise rather than powerful. A player could possibly purchase multiple 6th dots, possibly by getting a second archsphere. A Matter 6/Life 6 who ignored targets and duration could at worst turn everyone and thing in a room into gold forever. While it's deadly and dramatic, is it really worse than someone using forces 5/prime 2 to destroy just as much? A game including 5th dot spheres to begin with is generally prepared for that sort of thing to begin with, hopefully.<br /> <br /> While they still give off an archmage feel, they also feel a lot more down to earth, fitting a game that uses 5th dot spheres. Using those sort of effects almost always would give off paradox, even in a sanctum in some cases.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ignore Patterns - The archmage does not need a pattern sphere for effects including their archsphere. //This one feels the weakest and really only enables people who want to rush a 6th dot. I see it as matter 2/Life 3/Forces 3 being added to the archsphere which is barely a discount that blocks them from having a reason to purchase those spheres later on. Would enable stuff like cor 3 time 3 starter mages gaining the ability to deal actual magickal damage AFTER a 6th dot. Might fit a character who really likes one sphere but also wants to stuff XP into non-magickal<br /> stuff as well?<br /> <br /> <br /> Ignore Duration - The archmage choses their duration without cost for effects including their archsphere. // While it's powerful, at worst I seeit being used as aggravated damage plus as an 'exploit', but aggravated damage already fill it's role well enough that it shouldn't matter. Someone using life 5/matter 2 to kill someone by turning them into salt<br /> <br /> <br /> Ignore Targets - The archmage targets an entire area and spends successes to exclude targets for effects including their archsphere. // I'd treat it like forces 4-5 effects, where I use successes to exclude a target from an effect. Using a matter 2/life 5 effect, the archsphere would allow someone to turn an entire building's population into salt, including their cabal and self if they don't get the required successes.<br /> <br /> Dominate Quintessence - The archmage controls quintessence of their resonance as they see fit without requiring successes. // Resonance seems like a good limiter to stop someone from just taking everyone's quintessence without a roll. That said, concencrating enemies to then steal their quintessence sounds fucking awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> Inspire Wonder - The archmage may use their archsphere to create Wonders, using the sphere rating of Prime's wonder creation. // Using archforces 4 to forge a sword of lava in a volcano, a talisman that sends all heat in the area in the direction of the swing. Or, Using Archmatter 3/Prime 3 for mining a special mineral in deep space to make a grenade which explodes everything it hits into pure Quintessence. Or, ArchEntropy 4 to go on a quest for a legendary weapon that rots it's victims.<br /> <br /> <br /> Paradigm Sphere - The archmage refines their sphere and may teach it as an alternate sphere, like the Syndicate have done for Primal utility, Void engineers for Dimensional science and Virtual adepts for Data. // I imagine this wouldn't fit every game, and would require LOTS of discussion with the storyteller and have the largest exploitability. That said, seeing as they spent over a second fifth dot's worth of experience on it, and enforces paradigms, a bit of specialization shouldn't hurt. Having a celestial's Forces refinement be &quot;Divine Energies&quot; which focuses more on light and other related things while excluding more modern energies sounds worth it though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are there any that would be worth adding to it, or need significant changing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}